            "line": "A dice-cup left on a table with the stake still under it.",
            "gold": 1000
        }
    ],
    "people": [
        {
            "name": "Marta the Landlady",
            "unit": "town_innkeeper",
            "cell": [
                15,
                10
            ],
            "facing": [
                0,
                1
            ],
            "talk": {
                "hello": [
                    "Welcome to the Flagon. Sit where there's a seat; stand where there isn't.",
                    "You again! Good. Regulars pay their slate."
                ],
                "ask": [
                    {
                        "q": "What's the Flagon?",
                        "a": "The oldest tavern inside the walls. Older than the Cathedral, which the priests don't like to hear."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Who's worth talking to in here?",
                        "a": "Old Corrin by the fire has climbed the Tower and come down again, which is rarer than it sounds. The card table will rob you. The bard won't stop."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "A room for the night. Ten silver?",
                        "cost": 1000,
                        "requires_not": [
                            "inn_room_paid",
                            "home:room"
                        ],
                        "set_flag": "inn_room_paid",
                        "a": "Ten silver, and it's yours till you've slept in it. Room two, along the passage at the back. The blue rug, not the red: the red's the card sharp's, and he bites."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Let us keep room two for good (60 silver).",
                        "cost": 6000,
                        "requires_not": [
                            "home:room"
                        ],
                        "set_flag": "home:room",
                        "a": "For good? Sixty silver, and room two's yours whenever you're through that door: the bed made, the rug beaten, nobody else's boots under it. Sleep in it as often as you like. If you ever want walls of your own, the Steward up by the Margrave's hall has empty houses he'd sooner see lived in."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Is room two still ours?",
                        "requires": "home:room",
                        "a": "Still yours. Blue rug. I had the card sharp moved to the red one, and he's taken it personally."
                    }
                ],
                "news": true,
                "sells": [
                    {
                        "item": "ale_flask",
                        "restock": true
                    },
                    {
                        "item": "bread",
                        "restock": true
                    },
                    {
                        "item": "cheese"
                    },
                    {
                        "item": "red_draught"
                    }
                ],
                "shop": "Ale, bread, cheese, and a red draught for whoever lost the argument.",
                "job": {
                    "flag": "job:city_barrel",
                    "done_flag": "found:city_barrel",
                    "ask": "Need a hand?",
                    "offer": "Gunnar's late with my barrel again. His brewhouse is up the lane. Tell him Marta sent you, and tell him I said it like that.",
                    "accept": "I'll fetch it.",
                    "decline": "I'm here to drink.",
                    "thanks": "Up the lane, west side, smells of barley. You can't miss it. People try.",
                    "waiting": "Barrel?",
                    "hand_over": "One barrel, barely dented.",
                    "not_yet": "Not yet.",
                    "done": "Lovely. That's a round on the house, and coin besides. Don't tell the regulars about the round.",
                    "gold": 1000,
                    "item": "ale_flask"
                },
                "bye": "Mind the step on your way out. Mind it more on your way back in."
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "Old Corrin",
            "unit": "keep_watchman",
            "cell": [
                6,
                11
            ],
            "facing": [
                0,
                1
            ],
            "chatter": [
                "Seven floors. I got to seven. Then I sat down and came home."
            ],
            "talk": {
                "hello": "Sit, if you like. I don't bite. I used to. The Tower took that out of me.",
                "ask": [
                    {
                        "q": "You climbed the Tower?",
                        "a": "Seven floors. Every floor is a world. Then on the seventh I looked up and saw how far it still went, and I came home. Nobody here thinks less of me for it. I think less of me for it."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "What's the top like?",
                        "a": "Ask somebody who got there. If you find one, bring them here. I'll buy."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Does anyone not want to climb?",
                        "a": "Half this city. They came to the walls instead. There's a living to be made down here, and the Tower doesn't miss the ones who stay."
                    }
                ],
                "bye": "Go up if you're going. Come down if you can."
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "Wren the Bard",
            "unit": "drunk_elf",
            "cell": [
                13,
                16
            ],
            "facing": [
                0,
                1
            ],
            "chatter": [
                "♪ Fill the flagon, fill it high ♪",
                "♪ ...the Tower's tall but so am I ♪",
                "Lark sings in the street for coppers. I sing in here for ale. Guess which of us is warm."
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "a card sharp",
            "unit": "quant_monkey",
            "cell": [
                4,
                16
            ],
            "facing": [
                1,
                0
            ],
            "chatter": [
                "Friendly game? Very friendly. You'll hardly feel it."
            ],
            "talk": {
                "hello": "Cards? Dice? Conversation? Conversation's free. The rest isn't.",
                "ask": [
                    {
                        "q": "Play a hand.",
                        "a": "...And that's mine, and that's mine, and that, I'm afraid, is also mine. Again?",
                        "cost": 150
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Heard anything?",
                        "a": "Somebody's chalking crowns on walls. Somebody else is paying for it. I'd like to know who, so I can charge them."
                    }
                ],
                "bye": "Come back richer."
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "a caravan guard off duty",
            "unit": "bird_archer",
            "cell": [
                17,
                16
            ],
            "facing": [
                -1,
                0
            ],
            "wander": 2,
            "chatter": [
                "Forty days on the road. Forty minutes in here and I've spent it all."
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "a sellsword and his drink",
            "unit": "sword_monkey",
            "cell": [
                9,
                17
            ],
            "facing": [
                0,
                -1
            ],
            "chatter": [
                "One more and I'll go up the Tower. One more after that and I'll go to bed."
            ]
        }
    ],
